leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Spanish pet names carry the vibrancy, warmth, and rhythmic beauty of one of the world's most widely spoken languages. With over 500 million speakers across 20+ countries, Spanish names draw from diverse cultures — from European elegance to Latin American passion. When you choose a Spanish name for your pet, you tap into this rich cultural tapestry and give your companion a name full of life and character.\"]}]\ne:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Spanish names are also remarkably practical for English-speaking households. Many Spanish words are already familiar to English speakers — Bonita, Chico, Amigo, Fiesta — making pronunciation intuitive. The language's clear vowel sounds and rhythmic flow make Spanish names easy for pets to recognize and respond to. Whether you have Hispanic heritage or simply love the sound of Spanish, these names bring alegría (joy) to your home.\"]}]\nf:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Traditional Spanish Pet Names\"]}]\n10:[\"$\",\"p\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"These classic Spanish names have stood the test of time and remain beloved choices for pets around the world:\"]}]\n11:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Amigo</strong> — Friend. Perfect for a loyal companion. <strong>Bonita</strong> — Pretty, beautiful (feminine). <strong>Bonito</strong> — Pretty, handsome (masculine). <strong>Chico</strong> — Boy, little one. <strong>Chica</strong> — Girl. <strong>Cielo</strong> — Heaven, sky. <strong>Corazón</strong> — Heart. For pets who are your heart. <strong>Dulce</strong> — Sweet. <strong>Estrella</strong> — Star. <strong>Linda</strong> — Cute, pretty. <strong>Lindo</strong> — Cute, handsome. <strong>Luna</strong> — Moon. One of the most popular pet names worldwide. <strong>Perla</strong> — Pearl. <strong>Reina</strong> — Queen. <strong>Rey</strong> — King. <strong>Sol</strong> — Sun. <strong>Vida</strong> — Life.\"}}]\n12:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Nature-Inspired Spanish Names\"]}]\n13:[\"$\",\"p\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Spanish nature words make beautiful, evocative pet names that connect your companion to the natural world:\"]}]\n14:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Alma</strong> — Soul. <strong>Aurora</strong> — Dawn. <strong>Brisa</strong> — Breeze. <strong>Canela</strong> — Cinnamon. <strong>Cielo</strong> — Sky. <strong>Flor</strong> — Flower. <strong>Isla</strong> — Island. <strong>Lluvia</strong> — Rain. <strong>Luz</strong> — Light. <strong>Mar</strong> — Sea. <strong>Montaña</strong> — Mountain. <strong>Nieve</strong> — Snow. <strong>Paloma</strong> — Dove. <strong>Río</strong> — River. <strong>Rosa</strong> — Rose. <strong>Selva</strong> — Jungle. <strong>Sierra</strong> — Mountain range. <strong>Tierra</strong> — Earth.\"}}]\n15:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Spanish Food & Culture Names\"]}]\n16:[\"$\",\"p\",\"12\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Spanish and Latin American cuisine and culture provide playful, affectionate naming options:\"]}]\n17:[\"$\",\"p\",\"13\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Burrito</strong> — Little donkey, also the food — adorable for small pets. <strong>Churro</strong> — Sweet fried dough, for sweet brown pets. <strong>Fiesta</strong> — Party, for energetic, joyful companions. <strong>Mango</strong> — Sweet tropical fruit. <strong>Mojito</strong> — Refreshing and cool. <strong>Nacho</strong> — Playful and fun. <strong>Pepita</strong> — Little seed, for tiny pets. <strong>Salsa</strong> — Spicy and lively. <strong>Taco</strong> — Everyone loves tacos. <strong>Tamale</strong> — Warm and wrapped in love. <strong>Tequila</strong> — Spirited and bold. <strong>Tostada</strong> — Crispy and golden.\"}}]\n18:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"14\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Male & Female Spanish Names\"]}]\n19:[\"$\",\"p\",\"15\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Male Spanish Names:</strong> Alejandro, Antonio, Arturo, Carlos, Diego, Eduardo, Enrique, Felipe, Fernando, Guillermo, Héctor, Ignacio, Javier, Jorge, José, Juan, Luis, Manuel, Mateo, Miguel, Pablo, Paco, Pedro, Rafael, Ramón, Ricardo, Roberto, Rodrigo, Santiago, Vicente.\"}}]\n1a:[\"$\",\"p\",\"16\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Female Spanish Names:</strong> Adriana, Beatriz, Camila, Carmen, Catalina, Celia, Consuela, Elena, Emilia, Esperanza, Gabriela, Inés, Isabel, Julia, Liliana, Lucia, Magdalena, María, Marisol, Mercedes, Paloma, Pilar, Ramona, Rosario, Sofia, Teresa, Valentina, Valeria, Ximena, Yolanda.\"}}]\n1b:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"17\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Affectionate Spanish Nicknames\"]}]\n1c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"18\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Spanish speakers are famous for their warm, affectionate nicknames. These terms of endearment make perfect pet names:\"]}]\n1d:[\"$\",\"p\",\"19\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"<strong>Bebé</strong> — Baby. <strong>Cariño</strong> — Darling, sweetheart. <strong>Chiquito/a</strong> — Tiny little one. <strong>Gordito/a</strong> — Little chubby one (affectionate). <strong>Guapo/a</strong> — Handsome/beautiful. <strong>Hermoso/a</strong> — Gorgeous. <strong>Mi Amor</strong> — My love. <strong>Muñeca</strong> — Doll (feminine). <strong>Osito/a</strong> — Little bear. <strong>Precioso/a</strong> — Precious. <strong>Querido/a</strong> — Beloved.\"}}]\n1e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"20\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Explore our name generators for \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"32\",{\"href\":\"/animal/arapaima/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Arapaima\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"44\",{\"href\":\"/animal/american-black-bear/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"American Black Bear\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"67\",{\"href\":\"/animal/archerfish/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Archerfish\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"81\",{\"href\":\"/animal/american-bullfrog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"American Bullfrog\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"$L9\",\"106\",{\"href\":\"/animal/alligator-gar/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Alligator Gar\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" to find the perfect name for your companion.\"]}]\n1f:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"21\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"Frequently Asked Questions\"]}]\n20:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are Spanish names good for English-speaking households?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes, Spanish names are among the most accessible foreign-language names for English speakers. Many Spanish words are already familiar, and pronunciation is generally intuitive and phonetic.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What are the most popular Spanish dog names?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Luna, Bella, Max, Chico, Coco, Lola, Bruno, and Rocky are among the most popular Spanish-influenced dog names in the United States and Latin America.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Can I use Spanish names for cats?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Absolutely. Spanish names like Luna, Estrella, Bonita, and Gato (literally 'cat') are wonderful for feline companions. Their melodic quality suits cats' graceful nature.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Do Spanish names vary by country?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Yes, naming conventions can vary between Spain, Mexico, Argentina, and other Spanish-speaking countries. However, most common pet names are understood and used across the Spanish-speaking world.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-p